IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- s 4A: the specific classes of investors: "accredited investor" (s 4A(1)(a)), "expert investor" (s 4A(1)(b)) and
-- "institutional investor" (s 4A(1)(c)), the primary-residence rule of s 4A(1A), the Authority's power to modify them (s 4A(2)),
-- and one function that asks which class a person is in. Imports prelude, daydate, sfa-core and sfa-periods.
-- The amounts $2 million, $1 million, $300,000 and $10 million are the text's own numbers and are named constants below.
-- Where the text says "or such other amount as the Authority may prescribe in place of the first amount", the Authority's amount is an INPUT.
-- Money is in Singapore dollars: the text says "(or its equivalent in a foreign currency)" and gives no rate, so a caller who holds a
-- foreign-currency amount converts it first and states the Singapore-dollar equivalent.
-- "relevant person" is NOT defined here: it is a term of s 275 (Part 13), so this keel does not encode it.
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Every defined term of s 2(1) is ONE function, named `s 2(1) "<term>" <the thing> is <the term>`, over the facts a person could state.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--     JUST TRUE   the thing is within the term (a limb of the definition is met and no exclusion applies);
--     JUST FALSE  the TEXT says it is not: a definition that says "means" and no limb is met, or an express exclusion ("but does not include");
--     NOTHING     the text does not say: an "includes" definition (an open list) with no listed limb met.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "..."`; every branch that
--   answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A limb the Act hands to the Authority, the regulations or another Act ("prescribed", "specified", "as defined in the
--   Banking Act 1970") is an INPUT named for the fact ("the Authority has prescribed ..."), never a thing read from memory.
--   The definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires" (the chapeau of s 2(1)): that qualification is
--   `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` in sfa-definitions-rest.l4, not repeated here.

§ `s 4A: specific classes of investors`

-- src:4000 | 4A.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), unless the context otherwise
-- src:4001 | requires —
@ref s 4A(1) (src:4000-4001)
GIVEN
    `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the provision you are reading otherwise require a different meaning for the class of investor?
    `the Authority has prescribed a modification of the definitions for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed a modification of the definitions in section 4A(1) for the provision you are reading?
    `the class of investor asked about` IS A `Class of investor` @desc Which class of investor is asked about?
    `the person is an accredited investor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4A(1)(a) the person is an accredited investor` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is an expert investor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4A(1)(b) the person is an expert investor` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is an institutional investor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4A(1)(c) the person is an institutional investor` answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1) the person is in the class of investor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the context of the provision otherwise requires a different meaning`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): where the context otherwise requires, the text gives the word no other meaning
        IF `the Authority has prescribed a modification of the definitions for the provision`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to subsection (2)": the Authority's modification for the provision is not among the sources
        IF `the class of investor asked about` EQUALS `an accredited investor`
        THEN `the person is an accredited investor`
        IF `the class of investor asked about` EQUALS `an expert investor`
        THEN `the person is an expert investor`
        IF `the class of investor asked about` EQUALS `an institutional investor`
        THEN `the person is an institutional investor`
        IF (`the person is an accredited investor` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is an expert investor` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is an institutional investor` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) “accredited investor” means ...; (b) “expert investor” means ...; (c) “institutional investor” means ..."
        IF (`the person is an accredited investor` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the person is an expert investor` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the person is an institutional investor` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a class the caller could not answer, so the text is not applied to it

-- src:4003 | (a) “accredited investor” means —
-- src:4005 | (i) an individual —
@ref s 4A(1)(a) (src:4003-4005)
GIVEN
    `the person is within paragraph (iA)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4A(1)(a)(i)(A) (net personal assets) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is within paragraph (iB)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4A(1)(a)(i)(B) (financial assets) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is within paragraph (iC)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4A(1)(a)(i)(C) (income) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is within paragraph (ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4A(1)(a)(ii) (a corporation with net assets) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is within paragraph (iii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4A(1)(a)(iii) (the trustee of a prescribed trust) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is within paragraph (iv)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 4A(1)(a)(iv) (a person prescribed) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(a) the person is an accredited investor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is within paragraph (iA)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (iB)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (iC)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (ii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (iii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within paragraph (iv)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is within paragraph (iA)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (iB)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (iC)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (ii)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (iii)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within paragraph (iv)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb the caller could not answer, so the text is not applied to it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accredited investor” means (i) an individual ...; (ii) a corporation ...; (iii) the trustee of such trust as the Authority may prescribe, when acting in that capacity; or (iv) such other person as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:4007 | (A) whose net personal assets exceed in value
-- src:4008 | $2 million (or its equivalent in a foreign
-- src:4009 | currency) or such other amount as the
-- src:4010 | Authority may prescribe in place of the first
-- src:4011 | amount;
@ref s 4A(1)(a)(i)(A) (src:4007-4011)
`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(A) the first amount of net personal assets, in Singapore dollars` MEANS 2000000

GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the value of the individual's net personal assets other than the primary residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the individual's net personal assets other than the primary residence, in Singapore dollars?
    `the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the estimated fair market value of the individual's primary residence, in Singapore dollars? (0 if none.)
    `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the outstanding amounts in respect of any credit facility that is secured by the residence, in Singapore dollars?
    `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed another amount in place of the first amount ($2 million)?
    `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the other amount the Authority has prescribed in place of the first amount, in Singapore dollars? (Any number if none has been prescribed.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(A) the individual's net personal assets exceed the amount` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual` AND ((`the value of the individual's net personal assets other than the primary residence` PLUS (`s 4A(1A) the value of the individual's primary residence counted in net personal assets` `the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence`)) GREATER THAN (IF `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` THEN `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` ELSE `s 4A(1)(a)(i)(A) the first amount of net personal assets, in Singapore dollars`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accredited investor” means (i) an individual (A) whose net personal assets exceed in value $2 million (or its equivalent in a foreign currency) or such other amount as the Authority may prescribe in place of the first amount"
    -- The primary residence is valued by section 4A(1A), which says it applies "for the purposes of subsection (1)(a)(i)(A)" and so to this limb only.

-- src:4013 | (B) whose financial assets (net of any related
-- src:4014 | liabilities) exceed in value $1 million (or its
-- src:4015 | equivalent in a foreign currency) or such other
-- src:4016 | amount as the Authority may prescribe in place
-- src:4017 | of the first amount, where “financial asset”
-- src:4018 | means —
-- src:4020 | (BA) a deposit as defined in section 4B of the
-- src:4021 | Banking Act 1970;
-- src:4026 | (BB) an investment product as defined in
-- src:4027 | section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers
-- src:4028 | Act 2001; or
-- src:4030 | (BC) any other asset as may be prescribed by
-- src:4031 | regulations made under section 341; or
@ref s 4A(1)(a)(i)(B) (src:4013-4031)
`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(B) the first amount of financial assets, in Singapore dollars` MEANS 1000000

GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the value of the individual's financial assets, net of any related liabilities` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the individual's financial assets (deposits, investment products and the other assets in the definition of "financial asset"), net of any related liabilities, in Singapore dollars?
    `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed another amount in place of the first amount ($1 million)?
    `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the other amount the Authority has prescribed in place of the first amount, in Singapore dollars? (Any number if none has been prescribed.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(B) the individual's financial assets, net of related liabilities, exceed the amount` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual` AND (`the value of the individual's financial assets, net of any related liabilities` GREATER THAN (IF `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` THEN `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` ELSE `s 4A(1)(a)(i)(B) the first amount of financial assets, in Singapore dollars`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accredited investor” means (i) an individual ... (B) whose financial assets (net of any related liabilities) exceed in value $1 million (or its equivalent in a foreign currency) or such other amount as the Authority may prescribe in place of the first amount"

@ref s 4A(1)(a)(i)(B) ("financial asset") (src:4017-4031)
GIVEN
    `the asset is a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the asset a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970?
    `the asset is an investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the asset an investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001?
    `the asset is another asset prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the asset another asset prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(B) the asset is a financial asset` MEANS
    IF `the asset is a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970` OR `the asset is an investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` OR `the asset is another asset prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“financial asset” means (BA) a deposit as defined in section 4B of the Banking Act 1970; (BB) an investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001; or (BC) any other asset as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341"

-- src:4033 | (C) whose income in the preceding 12 months is
-- src:4034 | not less than $300,000 (or its equivalent in a
-- src:4035 | foreign currency) or such other amount as the
-- src:4036 | Authority may prescribe in place of the first
-- src:4037 | amount;
@ref s 4A(1)(a)(i)(C) (src:4033-4037)
`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(C) the first amount of income, in Singapore dollars` MEANS 300000

GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the individual's income in the preceding 12 months` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the individual's income in the preceding 12 months, in Singapore dollars?
    `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed another amount in place of the first amount ($300,000)?
    `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the other amount the Authority has prescribed in place of the first amount, in Singapore dollars? (Any number if none has been prescribed.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(a)(i)(C) the individual's income in the preceding 12 months is not less than the amount` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual` AND (`the individual's income in the preceding 12 months` AT LEAST (IF `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` THEN `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` ELSE `s 4A(1)(a)(i)(C) the first amount of income, in Singapore dollars`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accredited investor” means (i) an individual ... (C) whose income in the preceding 12 months is not less than $300,000 (or its equivalent in a foreign currency) or such other amount as the Authority may prescribe in place of the first amount"

-- src:4039 | (ii) a corporation with net assets exceeding $10 million
-- src:4040 | in value (or its equivalent in a foreign currency) or
-- src:4041 | such other amount as the Authority may prescribe, in
-- src:4042 | place of the first amount, as determined by —
-- src:4044 | (A) the most recent audited balance sheet of the
-- src:4045 | corporation; or
-- src:4047 | (B) where the corporation is not required to prepare
-- src:4048 | audited accounts regularly, a balance sheet of
-- src:4049 | the corporation certified by the corporation as
-- src:4050 | giving a true and fair view of the state of affairs
-- src:4051 | of the corporation as of the date of the balance
-- src:4052 | sheet, which date must be within the preceding
-- src:4053 | 12 months;
@ref s 4A(1)(a)(ii) (src:4039-4053)
`s 4A(1)(a)(ii) the first amount of net assets, in Singapore dollars` MEANS 10000000

GIVEN
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
    `the corporation has a most recent audited balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have an audited balance sheet (the most recent one is the one to use)?
    `the net assets shown by the most recent audited balance sheet` IS A NUMBER @desc What net assets does the most recent audited balance sheet of the corporation show, in Singapore dollars?
    `the corporation is required to prepare audited accounts regularly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation required to prepare audited accounts regularly?
    `the corporation has certified a balance sheet as giving a true and fair view of its state of affairs as of the date of the balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation certified a balance sheet as giving a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the corporation as of the date of the balance sheet?
    `the net assets shown by the certified balance sheet` IS A NUMBER @desc What net assets does the certified balance sheet show, in Singapore dollars?
    `the date of the certified balance sheet` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the certified balance sheet?
    `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
    `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed another amount in place of the first amount ($10 million)?
    `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the other amount the Authority has prescribed in place of the first amount, in Singapore dollars? (Any number if none has been prescribed.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(a)(ii) the corporation's net assets exceed the amount` MEANS
    IF `the person is a corporation` AND ((`the corporation has a most recent audited balance sheet` AND (`the net assets shown by the most recent audited balance sheet` GREATER THAN (IF `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` THEN `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` ELSE `s 4A(1)(a)(ii) the first amount of net assets, in Singapore dollars`))) OR ((NOT `the corporation is required to prepare audited accounts regularly`) AND `the corporation has certified a balance sheet as giving a true and fair view of its state of affairs as of the date of the balance sheet` AND (`period: the date is within a period before` `the date of the certified balance sheet` `the date asked` 12 Months) AND (`the net assets shown by the certified balance sheet` GREATER THAN (IF `the Authority has prescribed another amount in place of the first amount` THEN `the other amount the Authority has prescribed, in Singapore dollars` ELSE `s 4A(1)(a)(ii) the first amount of net assets, in Singapore dollars`))))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accredited investor” means ... (ii) a corporation with net assets exceeding $10 million in value (or its equivalent in a foreign currency) or such other amount as the Authority may prescribe, in place of the first amount, as determined by (A) the most recent audited balance sheet of the corporation; or (B) where the corporation is not required to prepare audited accounts regularly, a balance sheet of the corporation certified by the corporation as giving a true and fair view of the state of affairs of the corporation as of the date of the balance sheet, which date must be within the preceding 12 months"
    -- FORK F3 (NOTES.md): limb (A) is read as open to any corporation that has an audited balance sheet, and limb (B) only to one not required to prepare audited accounts regularly. The other reading confines (A) to a corporation that is required to prepare audited accounts regularly.
    -- "within the preceding 12 months" is counted by sfa-periods.l4 (convention P6: from the corresponding date 12 months earlier up to the day before the date asked).

-- src:4055 | (iii) the trustee of such trust as the Authority may
-- src:4056 | prescribe, when acting in that capacity; or
@ref s 4A(1)(a)(iii) (src:4055-4056)
GIVEN
    `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee of a trust that the Authority has prescribed for this purpose?
    `the person is acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting as trustee of that trust at the time in question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(a)(iii) the person is the trustee of a prescribed trust, when acting in that capacity` MEANS
    IF `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` AND `the person is acting in that capacity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accredited investor” means ... (iii) the trustee of such trust as the Authority may prescribe, when acting in that capacity"

-- src:4058 | (iv) such other person as the Authority may prescribe;
@ref s 4A(1)(a)(iv) (src:4058-4058)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed the person as an accredited investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the person (or a class that includes the person) as an accredited investor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(a)(iv) the person is a person the Authority has prescribed as an accredited investor` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has prescribed the person as an accredited investor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“accredited investor” means ... (iv) such other person as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:4060 | (b) “expert investor” means —
-- src:4062 | (i) a person whose business involves the acquisition and
-- src:4063 | disposal, or the holding, of capital markets products,
-- src:4064 | whether as principal or agent;
-- src:4066 | (ii) the trustee of such trust as the Authority may
-- src:4067 | prescribe, when acting in that capacity; or
-- src:4069 | (iii) such other person as the Authority may prescribe;
@ref s 4A(1)(b) (src:4060-4069)
GIVEN
    `the person's business involves the acquisition and disposal, or the holding, of capital markets products, whether as principal or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person's business involve the acquisition and disposal, or the holding, of capital markets products, whether as principal or agent?
    `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee of a trust that the Authority has prescribed for this purpose?
    `the person is acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting as trustee of that trust at the time in question?
    `the Authority has prescribed the person as an expert investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the person (or a class that includes the person) as an expert investor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(b) the person is an expert investor` MEANS
    IF `the person's business involves the acquisition and disposal, or the holding, of capital markets products, whether as principal or agent` OR (`the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` AND `the person is acting in that capacity`) OR `the Authority has prescribed the person as an expert investor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“expert investor” means (i) a person whose business involves the acquisition and disposal, or the holding, of capital markets products, whether as principal or agent; (ii) the trustee of such trust as the Authority may prescribe, when acting in that capacity; or (iii) such other person as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:4074 | (c) “institutional investor” means —
@ref s 4A(1)(c) (src:4074-4074)
GIVEN
    `the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(c) the person is an institutional investor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person is within s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii)` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a group of limbs the caller could not answer, so the text is not applied to it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“institutional investor” means (i) the Government; ...; or (xxvii) such other person as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:4076 | (i) the Government;
-- src:4078 | (ii) a statutory board as may be prescribed by regulations
-- src:4079 | made under section 341;
-- src:4081 | (iii) an entity that is wholly and beneficially owned,
-- src:4082 | whether directly or indirectly, by a central
-- src:4083 | government of a country and whose principal
-- src:4084 | activity is —
-- src:4086 | (A) to manage its own funds;
-- src:4088 | (B) to manage the funds of the central government
-- src:4089 | of that country (which may include the reserves
-- src:4090 | of that central government and any pension or
-- src:4091 | provident fund of that country); or
-- src:4093 | (C) to manage the funds (which may include the
-- src:4094 | reserves of that central government and any
-- src:4095 | pension or provident fund of that country) of
-- src:4096 | another entity that is wholly and beneficially
-- src:4097 | owned, whether directly or indirectly, by the
-- src:4098 | central government of that country;
-- src:4100 | (iv) any entity —
-- src:4102 | (A) that is wholly and beneficially owned, whether
-- src:4103 | directly or indirectly, by the central
-- src:4104 | government of a country; and
-- src:4106 | (B) whose funds are managed by an entity
-- src:4107 | mentioned in sub‑paragraph (iii);
-- src:4109 | (v) a central bank in a jurisdiction other than Singapore;
-- src:4111 | (vi) a central government in a country other than
-- src:4112 | Singapore;
-- src:4114 | (vii) an agency (of a central government in a country other
-- src:4115 | than Singapore) that is incorporated or established in
-- src:4116 | a country other than Singapore;
-- src:4121 | (viii) a multilateral agency, international organisation or
-- src:4122 | supranational agency as may be prescribed by
-- src:4123 | regulations made under section 341;
@ref s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii) (src:4076-4123)
GIVEN
    `the person is the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the Government?
    `the person is a statutory board prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a statutory board prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `the person is an entity wholly and beneficially owned, directly or indirectly, by the central government of a country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity that is wholly and beneficially owned, whether directly or indirectly, by the central government of a country?
    `the person's principal activity is to manage its own funds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's principal activity to manage its own funds?
    `the person's principal activity is to manage the funds of the central government of that country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's principal activity to manage the funds of the central government of that country (which may include its reserves and any pension or provident fund of that country)?
    `the person's principal activity is to manage the funds of another entity wholly and beneficially owned by that central government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person's principal activity to manage the funds (which may include the reserves of that central government and any pension or provident fund of that country) of another entity that is wholly and beneficially owned, whether directly or indirectly, by the central government of that country?
    `the person's funds are managed by an entity mentioned in sub-paragraph (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the person's funds managed by an entity mentioned in sub-paragraph (iii) (an entity wholly and beneficially owned by a central government whose principal activity is as described there)?
    `the person is a central bank in a jurisdiction other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a central bank in a jurisdiction other than Singapore?
    `the person is a central government in a country other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a central government in a country other than Singapore?
    `the person is an agency of a central government in a country other than Singapore, incorporated or established in a country other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an agency (of a central government in a country other than Singapore) that is incorporated or established in a country other than Singapore?
    `the person is a multilateral agency, international organisation or supranational agency prescribed by regulations made under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a multilateral agency, international organisation or supranational agency as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(c)(i) to (viii) the person is the Government, a government body or a central-government entity` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Government` OR `the person is a statutory board prescribed by regulations made under section 341` OR (`the person is an entity wholly and beneficially owned, directly or indirectly, by the central government of a country` AND (`the person's principal activity is to manage its own funds` OR `the person's principal activity is to manage the funds of the central government of that country` OR `the person's principal activity is to manage the funds of another entity wholly and beneficially owned by that central government`)) OR (`the person is an entity wholly and beneficially owned, directly or indirectly, by the central government of a country` AND `the person's funds are managed by an entity mentioned in sub-paragraph (iii)`) OR `the person is a central bank in a jurisdiction other than Singapore` OR `the person is a central government in a country other than Singapore` OR `the person is an agency of a central government in a country other than Singapore, incorporated or established in a country other than Singapore` OR `the person is a multilateral agency, international organisation or supranational agency prescribed by regulations made under section 341`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“institutional investor” means (i) the Government; (ii) a statutory board as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341; (iii) an entity that is wholly and beneficially owned, whether directly or indirectly, by a central government of a country and whose principal activity is (A) to manage its own funds; (B) to manage the funds of the central government of that country ...; or (C) to manage the funds ... of another entity that is wholly and beneficially owned ...; (iv) any entity (A) that is wholly and beneficially owned, whether directly or indirectly, by the central government of a country; and (B) whose funds are managed by an entity mentioned in sub-paragraph (iii); (v) a central bank in a jurisdiction other than Singapore; (vi) a central government in a country other than Singapore; (vii) an agency (of a central government in a country other than Singapore) that is incorporated or established in a country other than Singapore; (viii) a multilateral agency, international organisation or supranational agency as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341"

-- src:4125 | (ix) a bank that is licensed under the Banking Act 1970;
-- src:4127 | (x) a merchant bank that is licensed under the Banking
-- src:4128 | Act 1970;
-- src:4130 | (xi) a finance company that is licensed under the Finance
-- src:4131 | Companies Act 1967;
-- src:4133 | (xii) a company or co‑operative society that is licensed
-- src:4134 | under the Insurance Act 1966 to carry on insurance
-- src:4135 | business in Singapore;
-- src:4137 | (xiii) a company licensed under the Trust Companies
-- src:4138 | Act 2005;
-- src:4140 | (xiv) a holder of a capital markets services licence;
@ref s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv) (src:4125-4140)
GIVEN
    `the person is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a bank that is licensed under the Banking Act 1970?
    `the person is a merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a merchant bank that is licensed under the Banking Act 1970?
    `the person is a finance company licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a finance company that is licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967?
    `the person is a company or co-operative society licensed under the Insurance Act 1966 to carry on insurance business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a company or co-operative society that is licensed under the Insurance Act 1966 to carry on insurance business in Singapore?
    `the person is a company licensed under the Trust Companies Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a company licensed under the Trust Companies Act 2005?
    `the person is a holder of a capital markets services licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a holder of a capital markets services licence (as section 2(1) defines "capital markets services licence")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(c)(ix) to (xiv) the person is a licensed financial institution` MEANS
    IF `the person is a bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` OR `the person is a merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` OR `the person is a finance company licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967` OR `the person is a company or co-operative society licensed under the Insurance Act 1966 to carry on insurance business in Singapore` OR `the person is a company licensed under the Trust Companies Act 2005` OR `the person is a holder of a capital markets services licence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“institutional investor” means ... (ix) a bank that is licensed under the Banking Act 1970; (x) a merchant bank that is licensed under the Banking Act 1970; (xi) a finance company that is licensed under the Finance Companies Act 1967; (xii) a company or co-operative society that is licensed under the Insurance Act 1966 to carry on insurance business in Singapore; (xiii) a company licensed under the Trust Companies Act 2005; (xiv) a holder of a capital markets services licence"

-- src:4142 | (xv) an approved exchange;
-- src:4144 | (xvi) a recognised market operator;
-- src:4146 | (xvii) an approved clearing house;
-- src:4148 | (xviii) a recognised clearing house;
-- src:4150 | (xix) a licensed trade repository;
-- src:4152 | (xx) a licensed foreign trade repository;
-- src:4154 | (xxi) an approved holding company;
-- src:4156 | (xxii) a Depository as defined in section 81SF;
@ref s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii) (src:4142-4156)
GIVEN
    `the person is an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an approved exchange (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a recognised market operator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a recognised market operator (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is an approved clearing house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an approved clearing house (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a recognised clearing house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a recognised clearing house (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a licensed trade repository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a licensed trade repository (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a licensed foreign trade repository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a licensed foreign trade repository (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is an approved holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an approved holding company (as section 2(1) defines it)?
    `the person is a Depository as defined in section 81SF` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a Depository as defined in section 81SF?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(c)(xv) to (xxii) the person is an approved or recognised market institution` MEANS
    IF `the person is an approved exchange` OR `the person is a recognised market operator` OR `the person is an approved clearing house` OR `the person is a recognised clearing house` OR `the person is a licensed trade repository` OR `the person is a licensed foreign trade repository` OR `the person is an approved holding company` OR `the person is a Depository as defined in section 81SF`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“institutional investor” means ... (xv) an approved exchange; (xvi) a recognised market operator; (xvii) an approved clearing house; (xviii) a recognised clearing house; (xix) a licensed trade repository; (xx) a licensed foreign trade repository; (xxi) an approved holding company; (xxii) a Depository as defined in section 81SF"

-- src:4158 | (xxiii) an entity or a trust formed or incorporated in a
-- src:4159 | jurisdiction other than Singapore, which is regulated
-- src:4160 | for the carrying on of any financial activity in that
-- src:4161 | jurisdiction by a public authority of that jurisdiction
-- src:4162 | that exercises a function that corresponds to a
-- src:4163 | regulatory function of the Authority under this Act,
-- src:4164 | the Banking Act 1970, the Finance Companies
-- src:4165 | Act 1967, the Financial Services and Markets Act
-- src:4166 | 2022, the Monetary Authority of Singapore
-- src:4167 | Act 1970, the Insurance Act 1966, the Trust
-- src:4172 | Companies Act 2005 or such other Act as may be
-- src:4173 | prescribed by regulations made under section 341;
-- src:4177 | (xxiv) a pension fund, or collective investment scheme,
-- src:4178 | whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere;
-- src:4180 | (xxv) a person (other than an individual) who carries on the
-- src:4181 | business of dealing in bonds with accredited
-- src:4182 | investors or expert investors;
-- src:4184 | (xxvi) the trustee of such trust as the Authority may
-- src:4185 | prescribe, when acting in that capacity; or
-- src:4187 | (xxvii) such other person as the Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii) (src:4158-4187)
GIVEN
    `the person is an entity or a trust formed or incorporated in a jurisdiction other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity or a trust formed or incorporated in a jurisdiction other than Singapore?
    `the person is regulated for the carrying on of any financial activity in that jurisdiction by a public authority of that jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person regulated for the carrying on of any financial activity in that jurisdiction by a public authority of that jurisdiction?
    `that public authority exercises a function that corresponds to a regulatory function of the Authority under this Act or one of the listed Acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that public authority exercise a function that corresponds to a regulatory function of the Authority under this Act, the Banking Act 1970, the Finance Companies Act 1967, the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022, the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970, the Insurance Act 1966, the Trust Companies Act 2005 or such other Act as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `the person is a pension fund, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a pension fund, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the person is a collective investment scheme, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a collective investment scheme (as section 2(1) defines it), whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person carries on the business of dealing in bonds with accredited investors or expert investors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person carry on the business of dealing in bonds with accredited investors or expert investors?
    `the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee of a trust that the Authority has prescribed for this purpose?
    `the person is acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person acting as trustee of that trust at the time in question?
    `the Authority has prescribed the person as an institutional investor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the person (or a class that includes the person) as an institutional investor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(1)(c)(xxiii) to (xxvii) the person is a foreign regulated entity, a pension fund or scheme, a bond dealer or a prescribed person` MEANS
    IF (`the person is an entity or a trust formed or incorporated in a jurisdiction other than Singapore` AND `the person is regulated for the carrying on of any financial activity in that jurisdiction by a public authority of that jurisdiction` AND `that public authority exercises a function that corresponds to a regulatory function of the Authority under this Act or one of the listed Acts`) OR `the person is a pension fund, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the person is a collective investment scheme, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere` OR ((NOT `the person is an individual`) AND `the person carries on the business of dealing in bonds with accredited investors or expert investors`) OR (`the person is the trustee of a trust the Authority has prescribed for this purpose` AND `the person is acting in that capacity`) OR `the Authority has prescribed the person as an institutional investor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“institutional investor” means ... (xxiii) an entity or a trust formed or incorporated in a jurisdiction other than Singapore, which is regulated for the carrying on of any financial activity in that jurisdiction by a public authority of that jurisdiction that exercises a function that corresponds to a regulatory function of the Authority under this Act, the Banking Act 1970, ...; (xxiv) a pension fund, or collective investment scheme, whether constituted in Singapore or elsewhere; (xxv) a person (other than an individual) who carries on the business of dealing in bonds with accredited investors or expert investors; (xxvi) the trustee of such trust as the Authority may prescribe, when acting in that capacity; or (xxvii) such other person as the Authority may prescribe"

-- src:4191 | (1A) In determining the value of an individual’s net personal assets
-- src:4192 | for the purposes of subsection (1)(a)(i)(A), the value of the
-- src:4193 | individual’s primary residence —
-- src:4195 | (a) is to be calculated by deducting any outstanding amounts
-- src:4196 | in respect of any credit facility that is secured by the
-- src:4197 | residence from the estimated fair market value of the
-- src:4198 | residence; and
-- src:4200 | (b) is taken to be the lower of the following:
-- src:4202 | (i) the value calculated under paragraph (a);
-- src:4204 | (ii) $1 million.
@ref s 4A(1A) (src:4191-4204)
`s 4A(1A)(b)(ii) the most the primary residence counts for, in Singapore dollars` MEANS 1000000

GIVEN
    `the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the estimated fair market value of the individual's primary residence, in Singapore dollars?
    `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the outstanding amounts in respect of any credit facility that is secured by the residence, in Singapore dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4A(1A) the value of the individual's primary residence counted in net personal assets` MEANS
    IF (`the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` MINUS `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence`) LESS THAN `s 4A(1A)(b)(ii) the most the primary residence counts for, in Singapore dollars`
    THEN `the estimated fair market value of the primary residence` MINUS `the outstanding amounts in respect of credit facilities secured by the residence`
    ELSE `s 4A(1A)(b)(ii) the most the primary residence counts for, in Singapore dollars`
    -- FORK F2 (NOTES.md): the text takes "the lower of (i) the value calculated under paragraph (a); (ii) $1 million" and does not floor (i) at nought, so secured credit above the residence's value gives a negative figure and reduces net personal assets. The other reading floors it at nought.

-- src:4208 | (2) The definitions in subsection (1) may be subject to such
-- src:4209 | modifications as the Authority may prescribe for any specified
-- src:4210 | provision of this Act.
@ref s 4A(2) (src:4208-4210)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed a modification of the definitions in section 4A(1) for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed a modification of the definitions in section 4A(1) for the provision you are reading?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4A(2) the Authority has prescribed a modification of the definitions for the provision` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has prescribed a modification of the definitions in section 4A(1) for the provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be subject to such modifications as the Authority may prescribe for any specified provision"; with no prescribed modification there is nothing to apply
